  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Archives and Compression: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Archives and Compression: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bundle, Then Compress",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Many files",
                    "sub": "a folder",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "tar",
                    "sub": "bundle, no shrink",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "gzip / xz",
                    "sub": "compress stream",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".tar.gz",
                    "sub": "one file",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==tar== only bundles; compression is a separate layer, hence **.tar.gz**",
                "==gzip==: fast, good ratio, default; ==xz==: smaller, slower",
                "Both compress one stream, so use tar plus gzip or xz",
                "==zip== compresses each file separately; opens on Windows and macOS"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Compare",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Format",
                "Speed",
                "Strength"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  ".tar.gz",
                  "fast",
                  "universal on Linux"
                ],
                [
                  ".tar.xz",
                  "slow",
                  "smallest"
                ],
                [
                  ".zip",
                  "fast",
                  "cross-platform, per-file access; weaker Unix owner and permissions"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "gzip alone on a folder",
              "text": "gzip compresses ==single files== only. Wrap folders with **tar** first."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Two tools in one?** tar bundles, gzip compresses",
                "**One file from zip faster?** Per-file access; tar.gz decompresses from the start",
                "**xz over gzip?** When size matters more than time",
                "**Does tar compress?** No, only with z or J"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "tar: Create, List and Extract",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "tar: Create, List and Extract",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Mode Flags",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`c`",
                  "create"
                ],
                [
                  "`x`",
                  "extract"
                ],
                [
                  "`t`",
                  "list"
                ],
                [
                  "`f`",
                  "archive filename"
                ],
                [
                  "`z`",
                  "gzip"
                ],
                [
                  "`J`",
                  "xz (capital J)"
                ],
                [
                  "`v`",
                  "verbose"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`f` goes ==last== in the cluster, directly before the name",
                "Pick exactly one of `c`, `x`, `t`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create, List, Extract",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Create: `z` makes ==gzip==, `J` makes ==xz==",
                "==List first== when the archive comes from someone else",
                "`-C dir` extracts there; the folder ==must already exist==",
                "Name a member path to extract ==one file==",
                "GNU tar auto-detects compression, so `tar -xf` works for `.gz` and `.xz`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "tar -czf backup.tar.gz project/  # create gzip",
                "tar -cJf backup.tar.xz project/  # create xz",
                "tar -tzf backup.tar.gz  # list",
                "tar -xzf backup.tar.gz -C /tmp/restore  # extract to dir",
                "tar -xzf backup.tar.gz project/config.yml  # one member"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Archive name right after f",
              "text": "`tar -czf project/ backup.tar.gz` makes `project/` the archive name. tar fails on a directory; a file in that spot would be ==overwritten==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "gzip, xz and zip in Daily Use",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "gzip, xz and zip in Daily Use",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. gzip and xz",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "gzip",
                "xz"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Compress",
                  "`gzip file.log` → `file.log.gz`",
                  "`xz -k big.log` → `big.log.xz`"
                ],
                [
                  "Keep original",
                  "`-k`",
                  "`-k`"
                ],
                [
                  "Undo",
                  "`gunzip file.log.gz`",
                  "`unxz big.log.xz`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Plain `gzip` ==removes the original==, replacing it with the `.gz`",
                "xz levels: `-0` {green:fast} to `-9` {blue:smallest}",
                "`-9` uses ==a lot of memory=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. zip",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "zip -r site.zip site/",
                "unzip -l site.zip",
                "unzip site.zip -d out/"
              ],
              "note": "create, list, extract into out/"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Without `-r`, zip stores the ==folder entry only==, not its contents"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Read without extracting",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "zcat file.log.gz",
                "zgrep ERROR file.log.gz",
                "xzcat file.xz"
              ],
              "note": "view, search, view xz"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Originals vanish, files scatter",
              "text": "`gzip` on a log you still need deletes it: use ==-k==. `unzip` into the current directory scatters files: use ==-d== or `-l` first."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SSH Keys: ed25519, authorized_keys and ssh-copy-id",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SSH Keys: ed25519, authorized_keys and ssh-copy-id",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Key Pair",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Private key}: stays on your machine, ==never shared==",
                "{green:Public key} (`.pub`): goes on the server",
                "SSH proves you **hold** the private key without sending it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Generate and Install",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"you@laptop\"",
                "ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub user@host",
                "ssh user@host"
              ],
              "note": "writes id_ed25519 (private) and id_ed25519.pub (public)"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set a ==passphrase==: a stolen key file alone is not enough",
                "`ssh-agent` + `ssh-add` avoid retyping it",
                "`ssh-copy-id` appends the key as **one line** to server `~/.ssh/authorized_keys`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. ed25519 vs RSA vs Password",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ed25519",
                "RSA",
                "Password"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Key size",
                  "short",
                  "3072+ bits",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "fast",
                  "slower",
                  "n/a"
                ],
                [
                  "Status",
                  "modern default",
                  "legacy",
                  "{red:brute-forceable}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Copying the ==private key== to the server",
                "Pasting the wrong file: only `.pub` contents go in `authorized_keys`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Before disabling passwords",
              "text": "Test `ssh user@host` with the key first, or you may lock yourself out."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "~/.ssh/config, Key Permissions, scp and rsync",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "~/.ssh/config, Key Permissions, scp and rsync",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Config Aliases",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ini",
              "lines": [
                "Host prod",
                "  HostName 203.0.113.10",
                "  User deploy",
                "  Port 2222",
                "  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519"
              ],
              "note": "~/.ssh/config"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ssh prod` replaces the long command",
                "`scp` and `rsync` accept the ==alias== too"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Permissions SSH Enforces",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Path",
                "Mode"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`~/.ssh`",
                  "==700=="
                ],
                [
                  "Private key",
                  "==600=="
                ],
                [
                  "`authorized_keys`",
                  "600 (or 644)"
                ],
                [
                  "`config`",
                  "600"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Key readable by others: ssh refuses, `UNPROTECTED PRIVATE KEY FILE`",
                "Home or `.ssh` writable by others: server ==ignores== `authorized_keys`"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. scp vs rsync",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "scp",
                "rsync"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Upload",
                  "`scp file.txt prod:/tmp/`",
                  "`rsync -avz src/ prod:/srv/app/`"
                ],
                [
                  "Download",
                  "`scp prod:/var/log/app.log .`",
                  "same, swap the args"
                ],
                [
                  "Folder",
                  "`scp -r dir/ prod:/srv/`",
                  "built into `-a`"
                ],
                [
                  "Port",
                  "`-P` (ssh uses `-p`)",
                  "from the alias"
                ],
                [
                  "Re-run",
                  "copies ==everything==",
                  "sends only ==differences=="
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "one-off file",
                  "repeats, big trees, resume"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "rsync -avz --progress src/ prod:/srv/app/",
                "rsync -avzn --delete src/ prod:/srv/app/"
              ],
              "note": "-a perms, times, recurse; -z compress; -n dry run; --delete removes extras"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Trailing slash",
              "text": "`src/` copies the ==contents== of src. `src` copies the folder itself into the destination."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Archives, SSH Keys, scp and rsync",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Archives, SSH Keys, scp and rsync",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Archives and Compression",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Task",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "tar gzip",
                  "`tar -czf out.tar.gz dir/`"
                ],
                [
                  "tar xz",
                  "`tar -cJf out.tar.xz dir/`"
                ],
                [
                  "List",
                  "`tar -tzf out.tar.gz`"
                ],
                [
                  "Extract",
                  "`tar -xzf out.tar.gz -C dest/`"
                ],
                [
                  "gzip, undo",
                  "`gzip -k f`, `gunzip f.gz`"
                ],
                [
                  "xz, undo",
                  "`xz -k f`, `unxz f.xz`"
                ],
                [
                  "zip, undo",
                  "`zip -r a.zip dir/`, `unzip a.zip -d out/`"
                ],
                [
                  "Peek",
                  "`zcat`, `zgrep`, `xzcat`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. SSH Keys and Permissions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Public key goes into server ==~/.ssh/authorized_keys==",
                "`~/.ssh/config` block: `Host`, `HostName`, `User`, `Port`, `IdentityFile`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"label\"",
                "ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub user@host"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Path",
                "Mode"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`~/.ssh`",
                  "==700=="
                ],
                [
                  "Private key",
                  "==600=="
                ],
                [
                  "`authorized_keys`",
                  "==600=="
                ],
                [
                  "`config`",
                  "==600=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Transfer",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`scp -r -P 2222 dir/ host:/path`",
                "`rsync -avz --progress -n src/ host:/dest/`",
                "Dry run with `-n`; ==drop -n== to run for real"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Trailing slash",
              "text": "`src/` copies the **contents** only; `src` copies the folder itself."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
